-- #1382, the `ws:soundness` half — same mechanism as
-- `record_xmod_field_order/`, but the two colliding fields have DIFFERENT TYPES at
-- the swapped positions, so the wrong slot is not just the wrong number: it reads
-- an `Int` out of a cell holding a `String` pointer.
--
-- Expected output, derived BY HAND from the sources before anything was run:
--   zrmod: mkZ = Cfg { s = "zed", a = 44 }  =>  zrOut = "44" ++ "zed" = 44zed
--   armod: mkA = Cfg { a = 11, s = "arm" }  =>  arOut = "11" ++ "arm" = 11arm
-- so `44zed|11arm`.
--
-- Counterfactual, measured on THIS directory rather than reasoned: with
-- `compiler/types/typecheck.mdk` restored to `c5fda728` and nothing else changed,
-- `medaka build` on this entry still exits 0 and the produced binary dies with
-- `runtime error [E-FATAL-SIGNAL]: fatal memory fault (segmentation fault)` at exit
-- 139, having printed nothing.  (`medaka run` on the same shape was correct
-- throughout — that half was measured on the issue's own Repro B files, not on this
-- directory, and it is why the golden below was hand-derived instead of captured.)
import armod.{arOut}
import zrmod.{zrOut}

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (zrOut ++ "|" ++ arOut)
